abstract: >
  COMPASS (constrained objective multi-criteria performance, accountability,
  stability and saliency) is an open-source Python tool for choosing among
  trained models on more than predictive accuracy. It scores every candidate
  on performance (f_P), stability (f_S) and accountability (f_A), and selects
  the best-performing configuration that meets user-set minimum thresholds on
  stability and accountability. Shadow prices report the performance cost of
  each tighter threshold. The selection core is modality-agnostic. A bundled
  ECG use case covers cohort handling, a hyperparameter sweep, and saliency
  scoring.
